// ===========================================================================
// OBESITY — RECORDSET version. A complete, runnable policy.
//
// Height, Weight and BMI publish HISTORIES. They carry local codes, so they
// are ANSWERABLE — you answer a history by ADDING A RECORD (charter §3). What
// `shape is RecordSet` changes is not answerability but what the concept
// PUBLISHES: a set, not one record. So the reduction happens at the TOP rather
// than at every level.
//
// ⚠ AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS HEADER SAID `shape is RecordSet` MEANS "NOT A
// QUESTION", and that only `Obese` was a question. That was the retired
// "measurements are a thing you don't answer" mistake — corrected in
// `policy-layered.crl` and the charter and MISSED HERE (operator confirmed the
// missed sweep, 2026-08-29). It also conflated two different things: reducing
// to ONE RECORD (a `cpg-featureExpression` target) and being a QUESTION (a
// local `code is`). `obesityTarget.test.ts` warns against exactly that
// conflation, and already pins FOUR reachable questions for this option.
//
// ⭐ ONE OF THREE LEGITIMATE AUTHORING OPTIONS (operator, 2026-08-29), alongside
// `policy.crl` and `policy-layered.crl`. Not a variant of them and not
// subordinate: all are canonical, all owe the SAME truth table, and a lane that
// works for one and not the others is not done. The SAME four concepts are
// answerable in each. What differs is HOW you answer them — replace the one
// record, or add to a history — and how many publish a single value.
//
// ⚠ Keeping all three is also what makes `shape is` testable. It is a DISCRIMINATOR,
// and a suite declaring only one value of it cannot notice when the
// discriminator is ignored — precisely the open defect (step 6, "emit honors
// shape is"). It selects a different emitter path too: a reduction over a local
// `shape is RecordSet` OPERAND is gated explicitly (`cql-emitter/emitCQL.ts`),
// so `BMI`'s operands here are RecordSets where the other option's are Records.
// ===========================================================================
library "Obesity Coverage (RecordSet)".

terminology "Obese VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/obese`.
terminology "Clinical BMI VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/bmi`.
terminology "Height VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/height`.
terminology "Weight VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/weight`.

// THE question, and the condition. `most recent` is concept-level: it spans ALL
// THREE arms — the threshold computed over the newest BMI, existence of a coded
// Condition, and the local `code is` channel where an answer lands — selecting
// the one record this concept publishes. ⚠ The local code is an arm like any
// other; it is easy to overlook because no line of the definition names it.
concept "Obese":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `obese`.
- definition is "BMI" at least 30 'kg/m2', then most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Condition.
  - coded from "Obese VS".
  - value projection is exists this.

// ANSWERABLE like every coded concept — answered by ADDING a BMI record. Its
// records are the UNION of the computed values (over the Height and Weight
// histories), the recorded ones, and the answered ones. A RecordSet publishes
// its set, so no reduction is owed.
concept "BMI":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `bmi`.
- definition is body mass index of "Weight" and "Height".
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Clinical BMI VS".

// A history of measurements, and ANSWERABLE — you answer it by adding a height.
concept "Height":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `height`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Height VS".

// A history of measurements, and ANSWERABLE — you answer it by adding a weight.
concept "Weight":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `weight`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Weight VS".

activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVED`.

activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `NOT APPROVED`.

decision "Bariatric Surgery Coverage":
first:
- when "Obese" then recommend activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery".
